# S169 — empirical test of S168's 21% spike-block-fraction prediction

S168 prediction (paired with S74 k_* ~ N^{0.42}):
    sum_{sqf q in [2, Q*]} E(q, N) ~ 0.21 * pi(N),   Q* ~ N^{0.21}.

This script measures the LHS for d in {14, 16, 18, 20} and compares
to (i) 0.21*pi(N) and (ii) the SVD spike-block sum from S82.

## (A) Analytic cumulative sum vs 0.21*pi(N)

Computes  cum(Q) = sum_{sqf q in [2, Q]} E(q, N)  by direct Fourier
sieve (this is the LHS of S168's prediction).  Q* := round(N^{0.21}).

| d | N | pi(N) | Q*=round(N^.21) | 0.21*pi(N) | cum(Q*) emp | cum(Q*) main-term | ratio cum_emp / 0.21pi | ratio main / 0.21pi |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 14 | 16384 | 1900 | 8 | 399.00 | 530.67 | 531.80 | 1.3300 | 1.3328 |
| 16 | 65536 | 6542 | 10 | 1373.82 | 1739.54 | 1740.76 | 1.2662 | 1.2671 |
| 18 | 262144 | 23000 | 14 | 4830.00 | 6085.35 | 6086.87 | 1.2599 | 1.2602 |
| 20 | 1048576 | 82025 | 18 | 17225.25 | 20556.97 | 20558.60 | 1.1934 | 1.1935 |
| 22 | 4194304 | 295947 | 25 | 62148.87 | 72844.00 | 72845.71 | 1.1721 | 1.1721 |
| 24 | 16777216 | 1077871 | 33 | 226352.91 | 264244.37 | 264246.05 | 1.1674 | 1.1674 |

