## (B.1) Q at which cum(Q) matches the SVD spike block

If the spike block is the V_q^prim direct sum for some `effective Q*`,
then cum(Q_eff) should match the SVD spike block.  Solve for Q_eff.

| d | spike block | Q_eff | log Q_eff / log N | predicted = 0.21? |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 14 | 424.81 | 6 | 0.1846 | YES |
| 18 | 5087.28 | 10 | 0.1846 | YES |
| 20 | 18027.69 | 13 | 0.1850 | YES |

